The market place will always be dynamic and the external market changes.
Keeping up with the consistent market changes means structuring your company around the market and doing so faster than your competition.
The market today is filled with changes that can instantly put entire companies out of business and/or be displaced.
E-commerce companies that were using dubious tactics to trick Google search engines have been instantly penalized resulting in the collapse of their company over a period of just a few months.
Companies must be able to adapt to market environments and have preparation to ensure that their long term performance is sustainable.
One case to consider is Ford motor company.
The advancement of new technology made consumers seek an automobile with more features and sleeker designs.
The motor company was able to consistently keep up with the latest technology and outlived many interim competitors that failed to enter the market with any success.
Borders is a company that failed to properly implement a digital book strategy and rapidly fell behind in the R&D process and was unable to keep up.
It lost many of its loyal customers because they could no longer bear the urge to use digital e-books and switched to a provider that had them.
Trends are short lived and pursuing them can only distract a company from what will genuinely bring them profits year over year.
