Launch a brand, not product
Most of the companies start out by launching products, and that is their biggest mistake, they should have launched a brand.
When some brand has created a perception of trust, quality, and consistency, people are ready to pay more.
And when consumers trust a brand they become loyal, and by becoming loyal, they start buying more.
That is what happened with the POV video camera industry.
But Contour launched a product, fantastic product, and GoPro launched a brand that has defined that category now.
On the other hand, GoPro launched an aspiration for athletes to “Go Pro” and capture their spotlight moment with the brand.
And that is exactly why you should launch a brand not product.
Brands provide peace of mind.
Brands create difference and save decision-making time.
The branding is what allows us to pick certain peanut brand over some generic product.
That is probably because of the combination of the look, the feel, the quality and the brand’s stature in society.
Brands express who we are.
