10 traits that separate the best salespeople from others | Pro Business Plans
10 traits that separate the best salespeople from others
Extraordinary salespeople know they are crucial in today’s economy, and they will accept nothing less than being at the top of their game.
Although the work is not always enjoyable best salespeople succeed without guarantees.
These are some qualities that set best salespeople apart from the rest:
A good salesperson will always start with knowledge.
Although personality is very important when making a sale, being able to answer customer questions is much more effective because customers want to enhance the efficiency of their business, not to make a new friend.
The experience of selling a product is better when a salesperson believes in what they are selling.
If the sales representatives are passionate about what they are selling and are aware of the business improvement that comes whit the sale, their personality won’t matter that much and selling the product will be much easier.
When a salesperson has all the details that customer needs, even the ones that customer should have organized, there is more trust between the salesperson and the customer.
Nurturing the customer accounts they have inherited is not enough for good salespeople, they want to make new connections and figure out new ways to explore business with existing customers.
Rejection is not discouraging them, but it challenges them to find a new way to get the same end.
People skills are very important if you want to be an exceptional salesperson.
It can also help to know how much to share to build trust between the customer and salesperson or when to be less revealing to get the customer in the position of the seeker.
Complications are inevitable, and salespeople are obliged to help as soon and as efficient as possible when they occur.
If it happens that salesperson cannot solve the problem by themselves, they can always seek help from certain people in the company and resolve the problem in efficient and timely manner.
Instead, they take responsibility for their actions and are self-motivated.
On the other hand, needy salespeople waste a lot of their managers’ time, while they could just be on the field and learn from their mistakes.
They are always on time for customer meetings even when they are scheduling appointments with customers from different time zones.
One irresponsible salesperson is enough for the whole company to lose their reputation. Social awareness
They play the game, but with a high level of integrity and self-possession.
They are aware of who they are and what information they share at company events.
Good salespeople recognize the importance of being respected by their peers.
Because of this, they have learned how to recognize the customers in need of troubleshooting apart from the needy customers.
