The Most Important Investment You Can Make | Pro Business Plans
I often get asked by business owners and entrepreneurs what’s the single most important thing they should do to be successful?
It is without a doubt in my mind, the greatest investment that we can make, yet surprisingly few do.
They don’t develop skills, they don’t spend money on a coach or a mentor, they don’t travel to conferences or events, and they don’t take time out to recharge their batteries when they need to.
If these are the reasons they don’t, they will probably never have the time or the money in future.
For some people, this is a giant leap with little to no perceived value.
I remember one of the first skill development programs that I did cost me $15,000, which I didn’t have.
Upon reflection, it has easily been the single most valuable investment I’ve ever made, being a professional speaker now for many years and enjoying the financial reward that this career has brought me.
We need to be developing new skills, learning new ways of doing business, being inspired and developing our networks.
I’ve worked with many truly successful business owners and entrepreneurs, from all walks of life and all industries and they all share the common trait of working to improve themselves, both personally and professionally.
And interestingly, the more successful they become the more money and time they invest in learning and development.
It might surprise you to find out how much they invest and where they invest it – but I’m pretty sure they wouldn’t be doing it if it didn’t give a big return. SHARE
